 🕶️ We made it. Happy holiday weekend! Today's newsletter, edited by Herb Scribner, is 698 words, a 2½-min. read. Thanks to Sheryl Miller for copy editing .

 🚨 Scoop: The Trump administration is working on a post-war Middle East strategy. Now in the early stages of drafting, the plan is intended to guide the U.S. approach in the Middle East after the Iran war ends, Axios' Barak Ravid reports . 

 👀 Situational awareness: President Trump will use the Qatari-gifted Boeing luxury jet for his upcoming trip to Ireland — the first time he's used the plane overseas since his July catering-container escape in Turkey, the N.Y. Times' Maggie Haberman scoops. ( Gift link ) 

 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 1 big thing: Costly summer send-off 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Stock: Getty Images Summer's last hurrah will come with persistent pump pain and pricey burgers, Axios' Avery Lotz reports .

 Gas prices are almost certain to remain north of $4 per gallon over Labor Day weekend — a busy travel period that coincides with the intensifying midterm election season. ⛽ Labor Day gas prices are slated to be the highest on record, with market tracking firm GasBuddy and AAA predicting they'll surpass the previous high set in 2012.

 That's coming off a record-setting August, where the monthly national average of $4.07 trounced 2022's record, according to AAA data . ✈️ For travelers flying over the weekend, airfare is nearly 20% higher than last year, AAA says .

 Still, TSA predicts there will be more than 17 million travelers at airports across the country between Thursday and Wednesday. 🍔 A pound of ground beef costs $6.89 on average in July, up 10% from the year prior.

