 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 An LED sign welcomes U.S. service personnel in Pattaya City, Thailand, yesterday. Photo: Chalinee Thirasupa/Reuters 🚢 Vendors and travel agents swarmed crew members of the USS Abraham Lincoln, now deployed for a record 286 days, as they streamed into Thailand's seaside resort city of Pattaya during a port call that ends this weekend. Go deeper . 🏛️ A Massachusetts judge declared a mistrial in the Lindsay Clancy case after giving the defense extra time to make a last-minute appeal over the deadlocked jury. The defense argued one of the 12 jurors wouldn't budge due to a potential bias against mentally ill people. Get the latest . ☢️ A new watchdog report finds that Lori Chavez-DeRemer, President Trump's former labor secretary, drank on the job, misused government funds and oversaw a "toxic, intimidating and humiliating" environment, Axios' Avery Lotz reports . 🪖 U.S. military officials say they're turning off ad trackers on several devices over fears that commercially available location data has been used to target Americans in the Middle East, according to letters released today. Read the story ... Read the letters . 🏀 WNBA commissioner Cathy Engelbert will retire in December after leading the league for seven years, during a time of tremendous growth and widespread controversy. See the announcement . 
 
